WEBVTT

00:01.290 --> 00:03.000
<i>At the start
of the Alwas Playoffs,</i>

00:03.170 --> 00:05.010
<i>Molly and I totally bombed.</i>

00:05.880 --> 00:08.260
<i>It took the coaching
of superstar Rick Thunderbolt</i>

00:08.380 --> 00:10.050
<i>to put us back on track.</i>

00:11.800 --> 00:13.970
<i>And we made it big time.</i>

00:14.470 --> 00:16.640
<i>After four races,
we're now tied for second place</i>

00:16.810 --> 00:20.440
<i>with both Super-Racer and Aikka,
right behind the Crogs.</i>

00:21.360 --> 00:23.860
<i>To win our ticket to Oban
for the Grand Finals,</i>

00:23.980 --> 00:27.530
<i>all we have to do is stay
in the top three for two more races.</i>

00:27.780 --> 00:28.530
<i>Uh...</i>

00:28.700 --> 00:30.490
<i>Easier said than done.</i>

01:44.310 --> 01:45.940
Good luck, guys.

01:52.450 --> 01:53.410
HEY-

01:53.950 --> 01:55.780
So, Molly, according
to Rush's rule,

01:55.950 --> 01:58.580
is your ram's horn half empty
or half full today?

01:59.240 --> 02:01.710
It's full.
Definitely full to the brim.

02:01.960 --> 02:05.580
All right then, let's get out there
and kick some alien butt.

02:13.470 --> 02:15.800
You would think
I'd be more relaxed by now,

02:16.010 --> 02:17.640
but it's just the opposite.

02:17.850 --> 02:21.680
The higher we climb,
the more I fear our fall.

02:25.480 --> 02:28.480
Don Wei, you got to admit,
you're a real piece of work.

02:36.950 --> 02:39.120
For the fifth round
of the Alwas Playoffs,

02:39.280 --> 02:41.240
I call forth...

02:41.700 --> 02:44.250
the Earth team!

02:52.510 --> 02:55.550
Prince Aikka, have you come
to support the Earth team too?

03:00.310 --> 03:03.520
I don't make a habit
of befriending opponents.

03:04.350 --> 03:05.940
It can lead to disappointment.

03:16.910 --> 03:19.830
Challenged by Spirit,
ambassador of the Phils.

03:30.630 --> 03:33.420
I guess our reputation
is too much for him.

03:33.630 --> 03:35.260
He didn't even bother to show up.

04:00.280 --> 04:03.580
Correction, I think
Spirit forgot something,

04:03.740 --> 04:05.120
like his star-racer.

04:09.210 --> 04:10.920
That face.

04:40.860 --> 04:43.280
Hey, Don.
ls something bothering you?

04:57.670 --> 04:58.510
OK.

04:59.550 --> 05:00.590
Guess he's walking.

05:00.760 --> 05:02.430
Fine by me.
At least this will be painless.

05:11.980 --> 05:13.020
-Ah!
-What?

05:15.320 --> 05:18.360
What is that... thing?

05:32.620 --> 05:33.500
Impossible.

05:34.080 --> 05:35.340
It can't be.

05:36.630 --> 05:38.710
Everyone please be seated.

05:38.960 --> 05:42.220
<i>The finals of the first
interplanetary championship</i>

05:42.380 --> 05:44.510
<i>will start in just a few minutes.</i>

05:52.980 --> 05:53.980
Super.

05:56.190 --> 05:58.230
I'm counting on you, my darling.

05:59.480 --> 06:01.490
But don't be careless out there.

06:01.650 --> 06:03.570
Remember, it's only a race.

06:04.110 --> 06:06.700
Have you ever known me
to be careless, honey?

06:07.370 --> 06:08.450
Well, yes, I...

06:10.830 --> 06:12.160
Mommy, mommy!

06:12.500 --> 06:15.210
Please take me with you.
I want to ride in your star-racer.

06:22.300 --> 06:25.140
I'd love to, Eva.
But you know I can't, honey.

06:26.260 --> 06:29.060
Next time, it will be
just you and me.

06:30.810 --> 06:32.310
Do you promise?

06:33.060 --> 06:34.140
Promise.

06:39.070 --> 06:42.570
<i>Would the two finalists
please take their positions?</i>

06:59.790 --> 07:01.380
<i>Please give a warm welcome</i>

07:01.550 --> 07:04.470
<i>to our first finalist, Maya.</i>

07:04.760 --> 07:06.640
<i>She'll be defending
Earth's colors</i>

07:06.890 --> 07:09.640
<i>against the champion
of our alien neighbor.</i>

07:09.850 --> 07:11.890
Mommy's going to win,
isn't she, Daddy?

07:12.180 --> 07:13.560
Of course she is, Eva.

07:13.730 --> 07:15.940
You know Mommy's
never lost a race.

07:18.520 --> 07:21.110
<i>We have the pleasure
to have with us today,</i>

07:21.270 --> 07:24.650
<i>representing the Earth's
Coalition Authority,</i>

07:24.820 --> 07:26.860
<i>Governor McMillan.</i>

07:27.160 --> 07:31.450
<i>At his side, the leader
of the Clans Umbata</i>

07:31.620 --> 07:34.580
<i>and the Phils' First Son, Sirook!</i>

08:08.910 --> 08:09.820
It's him.

08:17.410 --> 08:18.290
That ship.

08:19.370 --> 08:21.460
It's impossible.

08:22.920 --> 08:24.960
What is it?
Have you seen it before?

08:25.960 --> 08:28.970
I know that wicked creature.

08:46.570 --> 08:49.030
No, no, no, no!

08:52.910 --> 08:55.950
Spirit, you will not escape me
this time. That's a promise.

09:16.390 --> 09:19.730
Do you remember when I told you
that I abandoned my wife

09:19.890 --> 09:22.690
and daughter after the crash
of my first champion?

09:22.850 --> 09:25.480
Yeah, well, sure, Don.
But I don't see the connection.

09:31.700 --> 09:34.490
That champion was my wife.

09:35.030 --> 09:36.530
Her name was Maya.

09:37.120 --> 09:37.790
Maya?

09:38.200 --> 09:41.160
She was one of the greatest
star pilots ever.

09:43.040 --> 09:45.590
That winged ship.
Of course.

09:45.920 --> 09:48.800
It was the alien she was racing
the day of her crash.

09:49.300 --> 09:51.300
How could I have
forgotten that ship?

10:01.730 --> 10:02.390
Coward!

10:04.150 --> 10:04.600
Molly!

10:08.650 --> 10:10.650
Hull protection down to 75%, sir.

10:10.820 --> 10:12.990
Molly, I want you
to race with extreme caution.

10:13.150 --> 10:14.950
This alien is very dangerous.

10:19.290 --> 10:21.410
Molly, what's going on
up there? Just drive,

10:21.580 --> 10:23.710
preferably in a straight line.
I'll protect us.

10:24.330 --> 10:28.550
We don't have a choice, Jordan.
If we don't get him, he'll get us.

10:30.210 --> 10:32.050
What are you talking about?

10:34.260 --> 10:36.050
This creature is evil.

10:36.470 --> 10:38.930
We have to get rid of him.
Trust me.

10:49.820 --> 10:51.940
I don't have anything
on my screens.

10:53.070 --> 10:54.400
Where is he?

11:08.290 --> 11:10.550
He's on the reactor.
Jordan, do something!

11:14.510 --> 11:16.800
Forget it, Molly.
I can't touch him from down here.

11:20.970 --> 11:22.850
Then I'll have to deal
with you myself.

11:24.930 --> 11:27.400
I couldn't care less
what happens to me,

11:27.560 --> 11:29.440
as long as you disappear
once and for all.

11:30.940 --> 11:33.070
Molly, don't do it.
Snap out of it!

11:33.530 --> 11:34.320
Pull up!

11:34.570 --> 11:35.570
Molly...

11:35.990 --> 11:37.070
No!

11:38.240 --> 11:39.030
Molly...

11:53.800 --> 11:55.920
Why is she taking
all these risks?

11:56.090 --> 11:57.510
I don't understand.

11:57.680 --> 11:59.550
It's as if he's taken
possession of her.

12:03.970 --> 12:05.640
Molly, stop this.

12:13.270 --> 12:15.280
Jordan, I need your help.
Try to reach her.

12:15.860 --> 12:17.110
Jordan?

12:22.990 --> 12:26.040
Koji, what data have you got
on Molly's physical condition?

12:27.660 --> 12:28.790
She appears OK,

12:28.960 --> 12:30.830
but her brain activity
is off the chart.

12:31.420 --> 12:33.130
She's not just angry,

12:33.290 --> 12:35.550
she's gone
completely off the deep end.

12:35.960 --> 12:37.720
It doesn't <i>make</i> any sense.

12:37.920 --> 12:40.260
<i>What could she have
against Spirit?</i>

12:43.970 --> 12:45.140
<i>Unless...</i>

12:45.430 --> 12:48.810
<i>she feels somehow
connected to Maya's crash.</i>

12:48.980 --> 12:51.400
Molly, I'm asking you
for the last time,

12:51.560 --> 12:52.810
come to your senses!

12:54.440 --> 12:56.570
<i>Could she be...</i>

12:57.190 --> 12:58.320
<i>Don Wei's daughter?</i>

13:00.660 --> 13:02.620
<i>That would explain everything.</i>

13:11.330 --> 13:14.340
Molly, or whatever
your real name is, it's Rick.

13:14.500 --> 13:16.340
I'm calling you
on the secure line.

13:16.800 --> 13:18.590
Stop hurting yourself.

13:18.840 --> 13:21.380
This is not what your mother Maya
would have wanted.

13:22.260 --> 13:25.010
My mother?
What do you mean?

13:25.470 --> 13:26.970
I know who you are.

13:27.140 --> 13:29.850
You're not alone in life.
You have a father.

13:30.020 --> 13:33.480
I don't know, maybe you two
can still find each other, start again.

13:33.980 --> 13:35.400
Whatever.

13:35.940 --> 13:37.940
Just don't do this.

13:45.200 --> 13:47.490
Uh, Rick. I, uh...

13:51.080 --> 13:52.290
Molly?

13:52.460 --> 13:54.460
Can you hear me?
Answer me!

14:07.720 --> 14:11.180
Don't come near me,
you murderer!

14:44.090 --> 14:46.220
I did what I had to do.

14:52.600 --> 14:53.730
What?

14:56.810 --> 14:58.900
Molly, Jordan, abandon ship!

14:59.020 --> 15:00.190
Do you COPY?

15:00.400 --> 15:01.650
The signal is dead, sir.

15:02.990 --> 15:05.240
I called for the rescue team.
They're on their way.

15:07.410 --> 15:09.660
Oh, Spirit.

15:09.950 --> 15:13.330
You can't have ruined my life twice.

15:34.890 --> 15:36.480
You have won the race, Spirit.

15:36.640 --> 15:38.650
You have no reason
to harm the girl.

16:09.300 --> 16:10.680
Here they come, Daddy.

16:10.850 --> 16:12.390
I can't see!

16:12.760 --> 16:13.720
OK, Eva.

16:13.890 --> 16:15.350
Time for a piggyback.

16:15.520 --> 16:18.600
-There. Is that better?
-Yes, I can see her.

16:18.770 --> 16:20.480
She's winning, she's winning!

16:39.580 --> 16:40.880
<i>Mommy...</i>

18:09.170 --> 18:10.170
Hey, Miss Wei.

18:10.340 --> 18:12.050
You gave us quite a scare.

18:16.470 --> 18:19.060
Wha... What happened to me?

18:36.030 --> 18:37.410
May I come in?

18:38.490 --> 18:39.490
Yeah, sure.

18:41.790 --> 18:43.370
I guess I messed up.

18:43.540 --> 18:44.670
Pretty much.

18:44.920 --> 18:46.210
Where are we now?

18:46.920 --> 18:49.050
The fifth round
hasn't finished yet.

18:49.340 --> 18:51.380
We'll drop at least
one place in the ranking.

18:53.800 --> 18:55.300
I'm sorry.

18:56.050 --> 18:57.430
That's not all, Molly.

18:57.850 --> 18:58.470
What?

18:58.800 --> 19:00.140
The Whizzing Arrow 2.

19:00.260 --> 19:03.270
Our only star-racer is
a complete wreck now.

19:03.430 --> 19:05.600
Stan and Koji are out
looking for parts.

19:05.770 --> 19:07.230
But who knows
where they'll find them.

19:07.400 --> 19:10.570
Oh. It was nice of you
to trust me this time.

19:10.730 --> 19:11.980
Whatever.

19:12.820 --> 19:14.650
What happened out there
anyway, Molly?

19:14.780 --> 19:15.910
You really freaked out.

19:16.070 --> 19:18.490
Do you know something
about this weirdo?

19:19.160 --> 19:21.620
Yeah, I thought that I did.

19:22.410 --> 19:24.750
But I was wrong. Sorry.

19:28.250 --> 19:29.960
Hey, why don't you get
some rest?

19:30.130 --> 19:31.920
We still have
one more race to go.

19:48.100 --> 19:50.940
You were right
about fearing the fall.

19:51.900 --> 19:52.900
What goes <i>up...</i>

19:53.440 --> 19:54.530
You OK?

19:55.490 --> 19:57.860
A lot of memories
came back today.

20:01.450 --> 20:05.040
Long-forgotten memories
that I thought... well, anyway.

20:05.290 --> 20:08.500
Watching Molly risk her life
against Spirit today

20:08.670 --> 20:11.130
made me think of my own daughter.

20:12.040 --> 20:14.760
Don Wei, human after all.
Who knew?

20:14.920 --> 20:18.130
Listen, there's nothing you can do
about your daughter right now,

20:18.300 --> 20:20.640
but you could be nicer to Molly.

20:21.100 --> 20:23.930
We've been pushing her
way too fast and too hard.

20:24.100 --> 20:25.350
She's just a kid.

20:26.850 --> 20:29.310
I'm afraid I don't have a choice.

20:29.560 --> 20:31.650
As soon as she's back on her feet,

20:31.810 --> 20:33.360
we'll need to push her even harder.

20:33.860 --> 20:34.900
I'm sorry to hear that.

20:35.070 --> 20:38.240
Do you really believe
in this Ultimate Prize?

20:38.400 --> 20:39.990
What is it, anyway?

20:41.200 --> 20:44.540
I'm under orders from the President
not to discuss it.

20:45.450 --> 20:48.500
We're like a billion light years
from Earth, Don.

20:48.620 --> 20:50.460
Can you give me a hint?

20:50.960 --> 20:52.380
It could help the team.

20:52.540 --> 20:54.590
And maybe even me.

20:54.960 --> 20:58.130
I'm afraid that they couldn't
bear the weight of it.

20:58.420 --> 21:02.340
The Ultimate Prize is unlike
anything you could ever imagine.

21:03.550 --> 21:04.850
Try me.

21:08.140 --> 21:11.230
The powers of the Avatar
are absolutely limitless.

21:12.980 --> 21:15.400
He can offer the winner anything,

21:15.940 --> 21:19.360
serving the Galaxy
on a silver tray, destroying worlds,

21:20.280 --> 21:22.200
even bringing back...

21:23.120 --> 21:24.530
...a loved one.

21:27.200 --> 21:28.540
Mommy.
